sequenceDiagram
    participant User as Data Scientist
    participant Gateway as data-science-gateway<br/>443/TCP HTTPS TLS 1.2+
    participant RBACProxy as kube-rbac-proxy<br/>8443/TCP HTTPS (Service CA)
    participant K8sAPI as Kubernetes API Server<br/>6443/TCP HTTPS TLS 1.2+
    participant Notebook as Notebook Container<br/>8888/TCP HTTP (localhost)
    participant CullingCtrl as Culling Reconciler
    participant ODHCtrl as ODH Notebook Controller
    participant DSPA as DSPA CR

    Note over User,Notebook: Flow 1: Notebook Creation & Access (auth-enabled)

    User->>Gateway: HTTPS/443<br/>Bearer Token
    Gateway->>RBACProxy: HTTPS/8443<br/>TLS (Service CA)<br/>Bearer token forwarded
    RBACProxy->>K8sAPI: SubjectAccessReview<br/>HTTPS/6443<br/>ServiceAccount token
    K8sAPI-->>RBACProxy: Allowed/Denied
    RBACProxy->>Notebook: HTTP/8888 (localhost)<br/>X-Auth-Request-User headers
    Notebook-->>RBACProxy: Response
    RBACProxy-->>Gateway: HTTPS Response
    Gateway-->>User: HTTPS Response

    Note over CullingCtrl,K8sAPI: Flow 2: Notebook Idle Culling

    loop Every IDLENESS_CHECK_PERIOD (default: 1 min)
        CullingCtrl->>Notebook: GET /api/kernels<br/>HTTP/80 (no auth)
        Notebook-->>CullingCtrl: Kernel list (JSON)
        CullingCtrl->>Notebook: GET /api/terminals<br/>HTTP/80 (no auth)
        Notebook-->>CullingCtrl: Terminal list (JSON)
    end

    alt Idle > CULL_IDLE_TIME (default: 24h)
        CullingCtrl->>K8sAPI: Set kubeflow-resource-stopped annotation<br/>HTTPS/6443 ServiceAccount token
        K8sAPI-->>CullingCtrl: Updated
        Note over CullingCtrl,Notebook: StatefulSet scaled to 0
    end

    Note over ODHCtrl,DSPA: Flow 3: Elyra Pipeline Integration

    ODHCtrl->>K8sAPI: Read DSPA CR<br/>HTTPS/6443
    K8sAPI-->>ODHCtrl: DSPA spec (S3 config, API endpoint)
    ODHCtrl->>K8sAPI: Read S3 credential Secret<br/>HTTPS/6443
    K8sAPI-->>ODHCtrl: Secret data
    ODHCtrl->>K8sAPI: Create ds-pipeline-config Secret<br/>HTTPS/6443
    K8sAPI-->>ODHCtrl: Created
    Note over Notebook,DSPA: Notebook (Elyra) uses ds-pipeline-config<br/>to connect to DSPA API and S3 storage
